<title>GERMANY: German winter grains, seeds crops await rainfall.</title>
<headline>German winter grains, seeds crops await rainfall.</headline>
<dateline>OFFENBACH 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>German winter crops need to receive more rain in February to make up for moisture deficits accumulated so far this winter, the DWD meteorological office said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;Milder temperatures and more sun could quickly exhaust the slim water reserves,&quot; a DWD source said.</p>
<p>DWD had received further reports of winter damage from the Brandenburg and Mecklenburg states in the East where snow cover was melting to reveal the extent of winter kill.</p>
<p>DWD forecast some rain and temperatures above zero and up to eight degrees over the next seven days across the country.</p>
<p>-Vera Eckert, Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
